From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:50:20 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: scaler: add the format, CSC and ratio encodings

The job path needs three pieces of register encoding that do not depend
on the hardware being present, so add them with KUnit coverage first:

- the formats the engine is known to take: 32-bit B,G,R,A (ARGB32 and
  XRGB32 in V4L2 terms), NV12/NV12M and P010, with their layout class,
  format code, subsampling descriptor and component order;
- the colour-space converter: a 3x3 Q3.12 matrix with input and output
  offsets (2^-24 of full scale, 26-bit signed), derived from the Kr/Kb
  luma coefficients of BT.601, BT.709 and BT.2020 for limited and full
  range, in both directions;
- the scaler ratio register, Q22 with the two lowest bits clear.

The tests compare against the register values used for the same
conversions in a capture of the engine on macOS 27 on an M4 Pro: all six
matrices and the offsets match bit for bit.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 224dd2bb08dee2a87ec205665343c5d8465a0d65)
